{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"923","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Producing Snow"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice likes snow a lot! Unfortunately, this year's winter is already over, and she can't expect to have any more of it. Bob has thus bought her a gift — a large snow maker. He plans to make some amount of snow every day. On day "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" he will make a pile of snow of volume "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Vi"},{"kind":"text","text":" and put it in her garden."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each day, every pile will shrink a little due to melting. More precisely, when the temperature on a given day is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Ti"},{"kind":"text","text":", each pile will reduce its volume by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Ti"},{"kind":"text","text":". If this would reduce the volume of a pile to or below zero, it disappears forever. All snow piles are independent of each other. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the pile made on day "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" already loses part of its volume on the same day. In an extreme case, this may mean that there are no piles left at the end of a particular day."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given the initial pile sizes and the temperature on each day. Determine the total volume of snow melted on each day. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ N ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of days. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"V1, V2, ..., VN"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ Vi ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Vi"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the initial size of a snow pile made on the day "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T1, T2, ..., TN"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ Ti ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"Ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the temperature on the day "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single line with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers, where the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th integer represents the total volume of snow melted on day "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n10 10 5\n5 7 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 12 4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n30 25 20 15 10\n9 10 12 4 13\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"9 20 35 11 25\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, Bob first makes a snow pile of volume 10, which melts to the size of 5 on the same day. On the second day, he makes another pile of size 10. Since it is a bit warmer than the day before, the first pile disappears completely while the second pile shrinks to 3. At the end of the second day, he has only a single pile of size 3. On the third day he makes a smaller pile than usual, but as the temperature dropped too, both piles survive till the end of the day."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"923B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/923/problem/B"}